e-personnel-safety walkthrough log — 2026-10-10
Worked-case lesson: no command line by design (brief §6).
The "run" is the travel-security briefing + workplace-violence prevention
procedure + lone-worker check-in design authored and self-reviewed in-session
against OSHA's workplace-violence guidance and OSAC's briefing resources.

Scope: fictional Kestrel Components (continued from e-media-protection /
e-physical-security): field engineer travel to elevated-risk region; two
aggressive confrontations at HQ reception by a terminated contractor.
Artifacts authored (all fictional, labeled):
  - Travel briefing: OSAC-sourced threat picture, twice-daily check-in with
    +2h/+4h escalation, pre-arranged transport, no-go areas, approved hotel
    criteria, emergency plan (consulate, medevac number, rally point), duress
    phrase with listener response; written acknowledgment; emergency contact
    briefed.
  - Workplace-violence procedure: zero-tolerance policy (posted, signed),
    per-site assessment (reception highest risk; late-shift warehouse second),
    engineering + administrative controls (duress alarm to guard's radio,
    paired staffing), training content, reporting channel with 48-hour
    investigation commitment and trust loop; the two confrontations logged
    as first cases.
  - Lone-worker check-in: arrival/midday/departure schedule, +1h/+2h
    escalation with named responders, schedule in shared calendar, the
    22:00 honesty test.

